Description: Tools for simulation and inference for matrix-variate Normal (MVN) and matrix-variate Skew-Normal (MVSN) models with complete,
	     interval-censored, and missing data. Provides functions for generating uncensored and censored matrix-valued observations,
	     evaluating likelihoods, and estimating model parameters via maximum likelihood, EM, and ECM-type algorithms. The implemented methods
	     cover complete MVN data, complete MVSN data, and MVN/MVSN models under interval censoring and missingness. Core functionality relies
	     on the skew-normal representation X = M + A|Z| + V, enabling joint modeling of skewness, censoring, and incomplete observations in
	     matrix-valued settings. Also includes the dj_data dataset, consisting of yearly 4 x 2 matrix-valued observations from 1920 to 1934,
	     for examples and methodological illustration.
